  "id": "DrugBank_DB09183 - MONDO_5354",
  "verbalization": "Dasabuvir is associated with Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection through a series of indications that collectively suggest a role in the treatment of this condition. The evidence shows that Dasabuvir is indicated for Hepatitis C Virus Infection, which in turn is indicated for Pibrentasvir, Beclabuvir, and Elbasvir, all of which are used in the management of Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection. This chain of indications implies a potential pathway where Dasabuvir may function as a component of a broader therapeutic strategy for Hepatitis C Virus Infection. The shared indication for Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection across these drugs suggests a common therapeutic goal, possibly involving antiviral activity or other mechanisms that target the virus. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Dasabuvir in the context of Hepatitis C Virus Infection treatment, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
